{"title":"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Ceva&#39;s_Theorem_sum_form)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Ceva's Theorem sum form)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Pi Academy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Ceva_Identity)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Ceva Identity)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be an interior point of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and extend lines from the vertices through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the opposite sides.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> denote the lengths of the segments indicated in the figure.  Find the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a81938ca5e71faa6894d9d52ac776c9efbe75d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/3/6535cb33f050aa34b71f21148dbad67ad56819a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c = 43$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/e/91e7679b01e114773e2822a8fd5615ea83def33c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 3$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:1988_AIME-12.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/a0/1988_AIME-12.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"234\" height=\"192\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Ceva.27s_Theorem_sum_form.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Ceva's_Theorem_sum_form)\">Solution 1 (Ceva's Theorem sum form)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Ceva&#39;s Theorem sum form)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cevian\" title=\"Cevian\">cevians</a> AD, BE, and CF. Using area ratios (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/8/458bae4d809ef768d59b1cb4ea8d8f895bc4149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PBC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> have the same base), we have: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/4/6d4ac85ad425625a41e117bcae717d10e8ad5d1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {d}{a + d} = \\frac {[PBC]}{[ABC]}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"125\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Similarily, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/f/47f2d984035fbfe5e48d693e2e43b890e55a66e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {d}{b + d} = \\frac {[PCA]}{[ABC]}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"122\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/a/54a5ecd6c3fa66bde1006a9a6a15a21e7b1a234b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {d}{c + d} = \\frac {[PAB]}{[ABC]}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"123\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>Then,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/4/1040a096ae433a59a04030b2b89c285891454e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {d}{a + d} + \\frac {d}{b + d} + \\frac {d}{c + d} = \\frac {[PBC]}{[ABC]} + \\frac {[PCA]}{[ABC]} + \\frac {[PAB]}{[ABC]} = \\frac {[ABC]}{[ABC]} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"532\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Identity\" title=\"Identity\">identity</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/a/a7a8154f8a98717671ee7423afc1add594861d76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {d}{a + d} + \\frac {d}{b + d} + \\frac {d}{c + d} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"212\" height=\"41\" /> is a form of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ceva%27s_Theorem\" title=\"Ceva&#39;s Theorem\">Ceva's Theorem</a>. \n</p><p>Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/e/91e7679b01e114773e2822a8fd5615ea83def33c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 3$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, we get \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/3/bd305fd0d0e48ac0b0330975c426104c87c34e3e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3}{a + 3} + \\frac{3}{b + 3} + \\frac{3}{c+3} = 1\\]\" width=\"206\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/4092762dabdb65624284e3cfe4b786c2f2d9bec3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3[(a + 3)(b + 3) + (b + 3)(c + 3) + (c + 3)(a + 3)] = (a+3)(b+3)(c+3)\\]\" width=\"481\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/5164a27c882483f2b05ae9bff9d3109389210a11.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3(ab + bc + ca) + 18(a + b + c) + 81 = abc + 3(ab + bc + ca) + 9(a + b + c) + 27\\]\" width=\"522\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/5/585be2e21d8c019bb5b64a5c1099ff541eef256c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9(a + b + c) + 54 = abc=\\boxed{441}\\]\" width=\"245\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy\">Video Solution by Pi Academy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Pi Academy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fHFD0TEfBnA?si=DRKVU_As7Rv0ou5D\">https://youtu.be/fHFD0TEfBnA?si=DRKVU_As7Rv0ou5D</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a9874ea56cf8fec1bd246793224fbcfaad17ab3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> be the weights of the respective vertices. We see that the weights of the feet of the cevians are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/9/3d91b4aeab7e3f27532148567103e553bd9256a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B,B+C,C+A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"167\" height=\"16\" />. By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mass_points\" title=\"Mass points\">mass points</a>, we have that: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/0/230d8e7d81ee0a8b4daae10daab18640f77b5fb1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{a}{3}=\\dfrac{B+C}{A}\\]\" width=\"89\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/6438187a2b2f4004aeadddca947722de1fdd09be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{b}{3}=\\dfrac{C+A}{B}\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"38\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/9/3099e8b2390d406b2d9e76b63d81e1aa0e3bb469.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{c}{3}=\\dfrac{A+B}{C}\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>If we add the equations together, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e2926a610bdbd1fff4983f55ff0c4aebdb5c07db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+b+c}{3}=\\frac{A^2B+A^2C+B^2A+B^2C+C^2A+C^2B}{ABC}=\\frac{43}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"473\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>If we multiply them together, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/1/001300542104d43310153c314fe93a49ed95b91f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{abc}{27}=\\frac{A^2B+A^2C+B^2A+B^2C+C^2A+C^2B+2ABC}{ABC}=\\frac{49}{3} \\implies abc=\\boxed{441}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"642\" height=\"39\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>You can use mass points to derive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a196f3a65a0a2585a18a952c4b5a25db8df27c80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {d}{a + d} + \\frac {d}{b + d} + \\frac {d}{c + d}=1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"217\" height=\"41\" /> Plugging it in yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/6/f66e8dde9dea71f049f82b63bd60935b847ccf90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{a + 3} + \\frac{3}{b + 3} + \\frac{3}{c+3} = 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"212\" height=\"39\" /> We proceed as we did in Solution 1 - however, to make the equation look less messy, we do the substitution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/0/2d07ee7331ed34b6dd472934872bd4bd96e1ff3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39;=a+3,b&#39;=b+3,c&#39;=c+3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"251\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/3/3d3e41ab2896c748e5aa24c1f67b0ebf31a68331.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{a&#39;}+\\frac{3}{b&#39;}+\\frac{3}{c&#39;}=1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"132\" height=\"37\" /> Clearing fractions gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/1/781ff4d213feff53e399946357de3695b48dc81e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39;b&#39;c&#39;=3a&#39;b&#39;+3b&#39;c&#39;+3c&#39;a&#39;\\to a&#39;b&#39;c&#39;-3a&#39;b&#39;-3b&#39;c&#39;-3c&#39;a&#39;=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"490\" height=\"15\" /> Factoring yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/f/a5fddd5991f6c1c196174aeee9fc2a8a2bbfea0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a&#39;-3)(b&#39;-3)(c&#39;-3)=9(a&#39;+b&#39;+c&#39;)-27,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"354\" height=\"20\" /> and the left hand side looks suspiciously like what we want to find. (It is.)\n</p><p>Substituting yields our answer as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/b/adb5988bf5a064298a10b364ff66218e749aa1ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9\\cdot 52-27=\\boxed{441}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"150\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Ceva_Identity.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Ceva_Identity)\">Solution 4 (Ceva Identity)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Ceva Identity)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A cool identity derived from Ceva's Theorem is that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddc19508a2bd455b2bebc78fb20c9b812a001550.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{AP}{PA&#39;}\\frac{BP}{PB&#39;}\\frac{CP}{PC&#39;} = 2 + \\frac{AP}{PA&#39;} + \\frac{BP}{PB&#39;} + \\frac{CP}{PC&#39;}\\]\" width=\"318\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>To see this, we use another Ceva's Theorem identity (sometimes attributed to Gergonne): <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/f/1ef7215290e55a139643d459623881358d97e287.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AP}{PA&#39;}=\\frac{AC&#39;}{C&#39;B}+\\frac{AB&#39;}{B&#39;C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"160\" height=\"40\" />, and similarly for cevians <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2ae0e30605dc87c83aecb3f588afa7129bee6aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BB&#39;$\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44b7058f8a28ca225136b284b337138a54e39e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CC&#39;$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />.  And then:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85ad5fa2e0e400e3ab82ae37c40b242af4bc851a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AP}{PA&#39;}\\frac{BP}{PB&#39;}\\frac{CP}{PC&#39;} =  \\left(\\frac{AB&#39;}{B&#39;C}+\\frac{AC&#39;}{C&#39;B}\\right) \\left(\\frac{BC&#39;}{C&#39;A}+\\frac{BA&#39;}{A&#39;C}\\right)  \\left(\\frac{CB&#39;}{B&#39;A}+\\frac{CA&#39;}{A&#39;B}\\right) = \\\\ \\underbrace{\\frac{AB&#39;\\cdot CA&#39;\\cdot BC&#39;}{B&#39;C\\cdot A&#39;B\\cdot C&#39;A}}_{Ceva} + \\underbrace{\\frac{AC&#39;\\cdot BA&#39;\\cdot CB&#39;}{C&#39;B\\cdot A&#39;C\\cdot B&#39;A}}_{Ceva} + \\underbrace{\\frac{AB&#39;}{B&#39;C} + \\frac{AC&#39;}{C&#39;B}}_{Gergonne} + \\underbrace{\\frac{BA&#39;}{A&#39;C} + \\frac{BC&#39;}{C&#39;A}}_{Gergonne} + \\underbrace{\\frac{CA&#39;}{A&#39;B} + \\frac{CB&#39;}{B&#39;A}}_{Gergonne} = \\\\ 2 + \\frac{AP}{PA&#39;} + \\frac{BP}{PB&#39;} + \\frac{CP}{PC&#39;}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"149\" />\n</p><p>Inserting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42c06de735d79f0b28c30bcbbcf96e67bb1ca42c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c, d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> into our identity gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/8/088741213ade8140e1f16e9bfd5ddf5c7d024068.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a}{d}\\frac{b}{d}\\frac{c}{d}=2+\\frac{a}{d}+\\frac{b}{d}+\\frac{c}{d}\\implies abc=d^3(2+\\frac{a+b+c}{d})=3^3(2+\\frac{43}{3})=\\boxed{441}\\]\" width=\"545\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>This problem is quite similar to the 1992 AIME problem 14, which also featured concurrent cevians and is trivialized by the identity used in this solution. For reference, below is a link.\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_14</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME\" title=\"1988 AIME\">1988 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1988 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1988\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tb